      en: "The Rumija Mountain Forest covers the eastern slopes of the Rumija range, a limestone barrier between the Adriatic coast and Lake Skadar. Dominated by holm oak, Aleppo pine, and Mediterranean scrub, the forest exhibits a mosaic structure due to karst geology and seasonal drought. It provides critical habitat for the Balkan chamois and golden eagle. The area is part of the proposed Rumija Nature Park, aimed at conserving its unique biodiversity. Human activities include traditional sheep grazing and limited timber harvesting.",
